# Notes on rules intentionally NOT ported as redirects:
# - www -> non-www: handled by a Cloudflare Redirect Rule at the zone level
#   (added Sep 2026, once www was registered as a Pages custom domain),
#   not here, since it's about which hostname resolves, not a path rewrite.
# - Extensionless URL <-> .html rewriting ("/page/" serving "page.html",
#   stripping ".html" from the visible URL): Cloudflare Pages already
#   serves clean URLs this way natively (it looks for "page.html" or
#   "page/index.html" automatically) - no _redirects rule needed.
# - 404 handling: Cloudflare Pages automatically serves 404.html from
#   the site root for any unmatched path - no ErrorDocument directive needed.

